      <main>
        <section class="ah-section" id="about">
          <h2>About Me</h2>
          <p>I am a third-year PhD student at the <strong>University of Science and Technology of China</strong>, currently pursuing research as an intern at the <strong>Beijing Institute for General Artificial Intelligence (BIGAI)</strong>, under the guidance of Professor <a href="http://staff.ustc.edu.cn/~qiliuql/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Qi Liu</a> and Researcher <a href="https://zilongzheng.github.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zilong Zheng</a>. I hold a bachelor's degree from Beihang University.</p>
          <p><strong>Open to collaboration.</strong> My research centers on reward modeling, LLM alignment, and continual learning. Feel free to reach out if you are interested in these topics.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="ah-section ah-interests-section" id="research-interests">
          <h2>Research Interests</h2>
          <ul class="ah-interests">
            <li>Reward Modeling</li>
            <li>LLM Alignment</li>
            <li>Continual Learning</li>
            <li>Agent Memory</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="ah-section" id="research-thrust">
          <h2>Research Overview</h2>
          <p class="ah-motto">“Toward language models that keep improving from their own experience — through better reward signals, robust alignment, and continual adaptation.”</p>
          <div class="ah-research-direction">
            <h3>Reward Modeling &amp; Alignment</h3>
            <p>Designing reliable reward models and preference-optimization methods that stay calibrated and aligned as the policy evolves beyond static training data (e.g., UAPO, SAVE).</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ah-research-direction">
            <h3>Continual Learning &amp; Memory</h3>
            <p>Enabling models to acquire, retain, and update knowledge over time through knowledge editing and ever-improving memory systems (e.g., ICE, RAM).</p>
          </div>
        </section>
